<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">British Isles</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British Isles are the group of islands off north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> made up of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>, Ireland and many smaller islands, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shetland">Shetland</a>. From the late 8th century Norse raiders and settlers established colonies there, and many of the settlers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faroe-islands">Faroe Islands</a> and Iceland came from these Norse communities or brought Gaelic companions and slaves.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-isles.jpg" alt="British Isles" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Schmaltz, MODIS Land Rapid Response Team, NASA GSFC (Goddard Space Flight Center) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MODIS_-_Great_Britain_and_Ireland_-_2012-06-04_during_heat_wave.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
